            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1055/s-0034-1383346</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Lichtenstein's hernia repair (LHR) is presented as a technically feasible procedure for inguinal hernia.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INDICATION" NlmCategory="METHODS">LHR is a standard procedure for open mesh techniques with very good postoperative results.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">We demonstrate an LHR step by step with preservation of the iliohypogastricus and ilioinguinalis nerves.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">LHR is a technically feasible and safe procedure which should have a firm place in a general surgical education.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Georg Thieme Verlag KG Stuttgart · New York.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
